      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{628d00a6b624bb0b622328ef|full_name} Hi, in Russian we use the small letter \"м\" (М - big, м - small) in most cases for meter. The latin \"m\" is also used, but very rarely since it is an international symbol.\n\nAlso, in latin writing, this “m” looks exactly like the letter “t” handwritten in cyrillic, so that there is no confusion, we use it less. (I have attached an image below)\n\nIf you go to the wiki page (meter) in Russian, the cyrillic “м” is used everywhere in the text\n\nin Ukrainian and Belarusian languages they also use \"м\" instead of \"m\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "65f562c8bacba1d91df1c2b5",
      "aiGenerated": false,
